    <title>Daily Digest 2026-10-22: Before you evaluate an AI SRE, give your existing ; Critical PHP Vulnerability (CVE-2026-109618, CVE-2; Today's PHP Security Release, and How We're Streng</title>
    <updated>2026-10-22T00:00:00Z</updated>
    <link href="https://islandirie.github.io/my-rss-feed/daily/2026-10-22.html"/>
    <content type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Before you evaluate an AI SRE, give your existing agent context&lt;/b&gt; — New or updated LLM releases affect tool choices across your entire stack — from IDE copilots to pipeline automation. &lt;a href="https://www.cncf.io/blog/2026/10/21/before-you-evaluate-an-ai-sre-give-your-existing-agent-context/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Critical PHP Vulnerability (CVE-2026-109618, CVE-2026-109619) &amp;amp;#x5b;infocon yellow&amp;amp;#x5d;, (Wed, Oct 21st)&lt;/b&gt; — Active threat or newly disclosed vulnerability — assess whether it affects your environment. &lt;a href="https://isc.sans.edu/diary/rss/33440"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Today's PHP Security Release, and How We're Strengthening PHP Security&lt;/b&gt; — Active threat or newly disclosed vulnerability — assess whether it affects your environment. &lt;a href="https://simonwillison.net/2026/Oct/21/php-security-release/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fragments: October 21&lt;/b&gt; — Flagged as relevant to your interests — read the summary to decide if it's worth your time. &lt;a href="https://martinfowler.com/fragments/2026-10-21.html"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;How we built ChatGPT’s novel ad stack for user trust and relevance&lt;/b&gt; — New or updated LLM releases affect tool choices across your entire stack — from IDE copilots to pipeline automation. &lt;a href="https://openai.com/index/building-chatgpt-ad-stack"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Show HN: Pawmc a.k.a. talking diary, an LLM chat with compartmentalised memory&lt;/b&gt; — New or updated LLM releases affect tool choices across your entire stack — from IDE copilots to pipeline automation. &lt;a href="https://pawmc-demo.kolaegipet.workers.dev/?demo=1"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Show HN: Embodsi – Embodied Super Intelligence&lt;/b&gt; — Community-vetted signal from Hacker News — high upvote-to-age ratio means the engineering community found it worth reading. &lt;a href="https://embodsi.com/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;There isn't an easy exploit for this PHP vulnerability&lt;/b&gt; — Active threat or newly disclosed vulnerability — assess whether it affects your environment. &lt;a href="https://eliastaylor.com/noexploit/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Your AI agent fixed the bug, but what else did it change?&lt;/b&gt; — Agentic tools are changing how software gets built — worth knowing what's newly available and battle-tested. &lt;a href="https://blog.trailofbits.com/2026/10/21/your-ai-agent-fixed-the-bug-but-what-else-did-it-change/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Using thousands of AI agents to uncover new leads in biological data&lt;/b&gt; — Design patterns and lessons from production systems — high-leverage reading for senior engineers. &lt;a href="https://openai.com/index/scaling-ai-research-for-complex-biological-data"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</content>
